From: bot-for-go[bot] <199222863+bot-for-go[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:33:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net/http: raise DefaultMaxHeaderValueCount to 32768

Go 1.27 added Server.MaxHeaderValueCount with a default of 500
(golang/go#79936). Repeated header lines count individually, and the
GODEBUG override was declined (golang/go#80020), so servers that
receive one header line per value break when rebuilt with Go 1.27.

Kubernetes is the main example: impersonation (Impersonate-Group) and
request-header authentication (X-Remote-Group, also used by the
aggregation layer) carry one header line per group. A kube-apiserver,
metrics-server or other aggregated API server built with Go 1.27
returns 431 for users with about 495 or more groups
(kubernetes/kubernetes#142606). The reproducing identity has 862
groups, and some users in the same directory have more than 1,000.

Raise the default to 32768, DefaultMaxHeaderBytes at 32 bytes per
header line. For lines of at least 32 bytes, such as one carrying a
36-byte GUID group ID, MaxHeaderBytes (default 1 MiB) remains the
binding limit, as it was before Go 1.27, and the count still bounds
floods of tiny headers. Servers that set MaxHeaderValueCount
explicitly are unaffected.

Add a test that the default accepts 15,000 repeated values and rejects
DefaultMaxHeaderValueCount+1, over HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2.
